      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for trying, but I don\u0027t understand how this can happen. You called `assertNoException` after calling `runVmTestService`. This means `runToFinish` has already returned, which in turn means either the executor was requested to shutdown (by the `onStopped` callback), or 300sec has passed (which doesn\u0027t seem to be the case for you; you spent only 6.6s).\n\nin crosvm.rs, the vm\u0027s state is set to `Dead` [1], \"BEFORE\" we call `onDied` [2], which eventually calls into `onStopped`.\n\nSo, above stack trace can happen only when we are running test methods concurrently. Are we? If so, force stopping wouldn\u0027t help though.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/android/virtmgr/src/crosvm.rs;drc\u003d2b65400f222409b205aba770564497220cb8f473;l\u003d554\n\n[2] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/android/virtmgr/src/crosvm.rs;drc\u003d2b65400f222409b205aba770564497220cb8f473;l\u003d574",
